// The shallows — the first slide where where you are is worth something.
//
// A water column seen edge-on: bright at the surface, dark at the bottom, still water, nothing
// else changed from `soup.ron`.
//
//   mm-cli run scenarios/the_shallows.ron --genome genomes/drifter.mm --ticks 50000 --check
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- why this slide exists
//
// `LightRegime::Directional`'s own documentation says what it is for — *"makes position worth
// something, and is the scenario that phototaxis has a reason to evolve in"* — and **no shipped
// scenario has ever used it.** `soup.ron`'s header says the same thing from the other side:
// *"Uniform daylight: no gradient to climb, so nothing here rewards moving."* Every world in the
// library is that world.
//
// The bill for it is in `docs/ECONOMY.md` §15.3, where the photosensor scores 288 of 1000, the
// chemosensor 288 and the cilium 288 — all three paying nowhere, and failing *together*. They
// have to: a sensor is worth what the information it returns is worth, and on a slide where every
// square is the same the answer is always "you are where you were" and the honest value of that
// is zero. The three are not separately broken. They are one missing world.
//
// It is worth being precise about what this does and does not test. Phototaxis needs a gradient
// *and* a body that can climb it, and §14 established that until `14.7` nothing in this engine
// could swim forward at all — a cilium's own wake outran its thrust. Every motility number
// predating that fix was taken on a body that could not move. So this slide is the second half
// of a pair whose first half only just landed, and a null result here means something different
// now than it would have a month ago.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the gradient, and its floor
//
// `Edge::Top` bright, so the gradient runs down the slide and a cell that climbs is going the way
// a reader expects. Full daylight at the surface.
//
// `dark: 96` rather than zero, and this is the choice worth arguing with. A floor of zero makes
// the bottom third of the slide uninhabitable, so the world becomes "a small bright slide with a
// dead margin" — a smaller `soup.ron`, measuring area again. A dim floor keeps the whole column
// live and makes the gradient a matter of *how well* rather than *whether*, which is the shape
// that rewards a cell for climbing rather than merely for not being unlucky.
//
// 96 of 1024 is under a tenth of full daylight. `docs/ECONOMY.md` §5 has the sweep this should be
// checked against, and its warning applies here too: a population on these slides oscillates, so
// one reading at one tick is a phase sample.
(
    name: "the shallows",
    seed: 20260812,
    width: 64,
    height: 64,

    light: Directional(bright: 1024, dark: 96, from: Top),
    current: Still,
    fluid_interval: 1,

    // The soup's chemistry exactly: this slide varies light and only light.
    seeding: [
        Uniform(chemical: 11, per_square: 409600),
        // The carbonate system (`docs/CHEMISTRY.md` §11). Carbonate matched to the dissolved
        // CO2 above, so the slide starts at pH 7 and every move from there is something the
        // cells did. Calcium is then *not* free: the pair precipitates on the product of the
        // two, so this is set to put `sqrt(calcium * carbonate)` a little over
        // `minerals.calcite_saturation` — near enough to equilibrium that the pH decides which
        // way it goes, which is the whole point of the coupling.
        Uniform(chemical: 18, per_square: 409600),
        Uniform(chemical: 17, per_square: 3461),
        Uniform(chemical: 14, per_square: 409600),
        Uniform(chemical: 4, per_square: 409600),
        // The three minerals nothing in the engine produces (`docs/CHEMISTRY.md` §8): seeding is
        // the only way in, and without them a nucleus, an enzyme or a shell cannot be built at
        // all. At the Redfield proportion of this world's own carbon — 16/106 nitrogen, 1/106
        // phosphorus rounded up — and half that again in silicon, matching the fresh slide.
        Uniform(chemical: 5, per_square: 61440),
        Uniform(chemical: 6, per_square: 4096),
        // The inert pool a diazosome cracks. Four times the bioavailable nitrogen: a
        // young world is mostly locked up, and unlocking it is what the organelle is for.
        Uniform(chemical: 16, per_square: 245760),
        Uniform(chemical: 7, per_square: 20480),
    ],
    barriers: [],
)
